course: dictionary
lesson: 11491
title: Words that make things worse
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aggravate is a verb, and it means to make a problem, injury or illness worse. If you pick at a scab, the cut gets worse. The context tells you what happens.
explain: «Running on a sprained ankle can aggravate the injury.» The clue is the word injury and the fact that running makes it hurt more. So aggravate means to make the injury worse, not to heal it.
explain: Aggravate also has an informal meaning: to annoy someone. «Stop aggravating your sister!» The clue is the telling-off, which means she is being annoyed. Try both meanings in the sentence: which one still makes sense?
fact: Aggravate is a verb: aggravate, aggravates, aggravated, aggravating.
fact: «Aggravate» means to make a problem, injury or illness worse.
fact: In everyday talk, «aggravate» means to annoy someone. This use is informal, so it is fine in chat but not in formal writing.
fact: «Aggravated» means made worse, and «aggravating» means annoying, as in «an aggravating delay».
fact: In law, «aggravated assault» is a more serious crime than an ordinary assault.
exercise: «Running can aggravate a sprained ankle.» What does aggravate mean here? | To make the ankle better | *To make the injury worse | To forget about the ankle | To tell someone about the ankle
exercise: «Stop aggravating your sister!» What does aggravating mean here? | To help her with her homework | *To annoy her | To hug her | To be quiet next to her
exercise: Find the word in «The dusty room aggravated her cough.» that means made worse. | dusty | *aggravated | cough | room
test: «Her little brother kept aggravating her by poking her.» What does aggravating mean here? | *Annoying her | Sleeping nearby | Helping her | Singing loudly
test: «Adam found the slow wifi very aggravating.» What does aggravating mean? | Funny | *Annoying | Quiet | Fast
exam: «Ravi kept picking at his scab, which aggravated the cut.» What does aggravated mean? | Cleaned the cut | *Made the cut worse | Made the cut feel better | Covered the cut
